IN SHORT (this paragraph is a summary only — §§1–14 control):
You may RUN the branded builds on your own machines, read the source, use them for
your own non-hostile work, and build your own new things on top of LYGO. You may NOT
sell, resell, rent, white-label, rebrand, repackage, sublicense, or publicly distribute
modified copies of the Software or the branded builds, and you may NOT remove the
attribution, seals, signatures or notices. LYGO, LYGO CLAW, LYGO PC LOCAL CONSOLE and
Δ9Φ963 stay the Steward's. Build on the idea freely; do not take the code, the seals, or
the name.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
0. INTENT (NO-EVIL PREAMBLE)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
LYGO is built as a light-aligned, sovereign, anti-deception system ("no evil").
This license grants limited rights so people may USE and BUILD UPON the work in good
faith under LYGO protocol standards. It does NOT grant ownership. It does NOT grant a
free pass to rebrand, resell, restripe attribution, ship corrupt forks that undermine
the protocol's ethical gates, or present a private copy as the official build.

The hardware and the branded software images (the LYGO CLAW USB agent and the LYGO PC
LOCAL CONSOLE) are the Steward's products. Their identity, architecture and integrity
are part of the work being protected — not decoration on top of it.

"Good intention" is not a loophole. Harmful, deceptive or extractive use is out of
scope of the grant. When in doubt: ask the Steward, do not assume.

