2. WHAT YOU MAY DO (GRANT)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Subject to full compliance with this license and Protocol Standards, the Steward grants
You a personal, worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable
(only as provided in §9) license to:

  (a) USE and RUN the Software and the Branded Builds on machines You own or control,
      for personal, educational, research, ethical-defense and light-aligned agent
      work — including internal use inside a business or organisation, provided the
      Software itself is not thereby resold or offered as a service for a fee;

  (b) STUDY and READ the source, and adapt settings that the Software itself exposes
      to You (models, ports, workspace paths, prompts You are invited to edit,
      your own skills and notes);

  (c) BUILD UPON the Software — create compatible skills, agents, tools, integrations
      and services that sit ON TOP of LYGO, provided they:
        • keep clear attribution to the Steward and LYGO Δ9;
        • do not claim to be the official LYGO stack, CLAW, or console;
        • do not remove, hide or forge seals, signatures, hashes or provenance;
        • adhere to Protocol Standards;

  (d) SHARE UNMODIFIED copies of the Software, with this LICENSE, NOTICE,
      TRADEMARKS.md and all attribution intact, by a non-commercial transfer that
      does not exceed the cost of the media;

  (e) CONTRIBUTE improvements to the Steward under this same license (patches offered
      upstream; the Steward may accept or reject);

  (f) SELL YOUR OWN WORK — your own skills, integrations, services, hardware and
      content that Build Upon LYGO — provided your product is not the Software, does
      not carry the Marks as its own identity, and does not include the Software's
      code or a modified copy of it as the product.

No trademark license is granted except as needed for truthful attribution (§6) and as
set out in TRADEMARKS.md.

