  (i) SUBLICENSE the Software under MIT, MIT-0, Apache, BSD, GPL or any terms more
      permissive than this license in a way that extinguishes these limits, or
      relicense it for others;

  (j) REMOVE, bypass or disable the integrity and identity checks described in §4.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
4. BRANDED BUILDS: IDENTITY AND INTEGRITY
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  (a) A Branded Build is delivered as-is. You may configure it through the settings it
      exposes and You may add Your own data, skills and notes, but You may not
      redistribute a modified Branded Build, nor publish a "fixed", "unlocked",
      "debloated", "relicensed", "generic" or otherwise altered version of it.

  (b) If You modify a Branded Build, it stops being a LYGO Certified Build. You must
      not continue to present it as LYGO, LYGO CLAW, LYGO PC LOCAL CONSOLE, "official",
      "certified", or "unmodified", and You must not keep the Marks on it in any way
      that suggests the Steward produced or endorses that copy.

  (c) You may verify the copy You hold and must not obstruct others from doing so:
      every Branded Build ships a machine-readable manifest of its files and a
      Resonance Signature. A copy whose hashes do not match, or whose signature has
      been altered, is UNCERTIFIED and must not be redistributed or sold.

  (d) Copies made for archival, backup, forensic or security-research purposes are
      permitted, provided they are not published, sold or offered as above, and
      provided findings are reported to the Steward rather than exploited.

  (e) Hardware: the LYGO CLAW USB device, its labels, enclosure, serial identity and
      pre-loaded image are part of the Branded Build. Reselling, reflashing for sale,
      or relabeling hardware as Your own product requires written permission.

