12. SUCCESSION, SOVEREIGNTY LOCK, AND POSTHUMOUS PROTECTION
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  (a) GRANT IS IRREVOCABLE FOR THE COPYRIGHT TERM. The licence granted in §2 is
      irrevocable by any third party and may not be modified, narrowed or replaced by
      anyone other than the Steward acting in writing. It remains in force for the full
      duration of copyright (in the United States, the life of the author plus seventy
      years; elsewhere, the applicable term) and does not lapse on the Steward's death,
      incapacity, or withdrawal from public activity.

  (b) SUCCESSION. The Steward designates one or more Successor Stewards (a trusted
      natural person, a foundation, a trust, or an entity created for this purpose),
      named in a written instrument and/or in a SUCCESSION file in this repository and
      in the Steward's estate documents. On the Steward's death or incapacity, all
      stewardship rights, enforcement rights and marks pass to the Successor Steward,
      who holds them in trust for the same purpose: to keep the original architecture
      pure, the provenance truthful, and the name hers.

  (c) NO ESTATE-BY-DEFAULT. Absent different written instructions, the Successor
      Steward may not relicense the Software under permissive or open-source terms, may
      not sell the Marks or the copyright out of the trust, and may not waive §2–§7.
      Any attempt by an estate, heir, receiver, creditor or acquirer to relicense the
      Software in a way more permissive than this license is void under this license's
      terms and will be contested.

  (d) CANONICAL SOURCE. The Steward (and thereafter the Successor Steward) maintains
      the canonical repository and the canonical signatures. Mirrors must always point
      to it. If the canonical source is lost, no fork inherits legality from
      convenience — provenance is what makes a build LYGO.

  (e) MORAL RIGHTS. The Steward's rights of attribution and of integrity of the work
      are asserted and, so far as the law allows, are perpetual and not waivable. Every
      copy, in every form, must keep the authorship attribution of §6 and must not be
      distorted, mutilated or presented in a way that is prejudicial to the author's
      honour or reputation.

  (f) IF NO SUCCESSOR CAN ACT. Then this license continues unchanged: the grant of §2
      and the prohibitions of §3–§4 remain in force, the Marks remain the property of
      the Steward's estate/trust, and no party may claim stewardship, relicence, or
      certify LYGO builds. The lock is that the terms outlive the author.

  (g) Nothing in this section is intended to violate the law of any jurisdiction;
      where a provision cannot be enforced, it is to be enforced to the maximum extent
      permitted, and the rest of this license stands.

